git connection 

install sudo apt update && sudo apt install git -y

1. check git config name,email
=> git config user.name 
=> git config user.email

if it is not there , run it 
git config --global user.name "Your name"
git config --global user.email "Your.email@exmaple.com"



2. move ~/ssh
=> ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "Your.email@example.com" (github)
=> cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

github project -> Settings -> SSH and GPG keys -> New SSH key

3. test 
=> ssh -T git@github.com


